unket In Touch</source><year>2001</year><fpage>10</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Ministry of Health</collab></person-group><source>Breastfeeding: A Guide to Action</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Wellington , Ministry of Health</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Patton</surname><given-names>MQ</given-names></name></person-group><source>Qualitative Evaluation and Research Methods</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>Newbury Park , Sage Publications</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rice</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Ezzy</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><source>Qualitative Research Methods: A Health Focus</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>Melbourne , Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hogwood</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gunn</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><source>Policy Analysis for the Real World</source><year>1984</year><publisher-name>Oxford , Oxford University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B28"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Hupe</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><source>Implementing Public Policy</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>London , Sage Publications</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B29"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Collins</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Hunter</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Health sector reform and the interpretation of policy context</article-title><source>Health Policy</source><year>1999</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>68</fpage><lpage>83</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0168-8510(99)00003-2</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B30"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blank</surname><given-names>RH</given-names></name><name><surname>Burau</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><source>Comparative Health Policy</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>Houndmills , Palgrave Macmillan</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B31"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gauld</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><source>Comparative Health Policy in the Asia-Pacific</source><year>2005</year><publisher-name>Maidenhead , Open University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>